  "strategyText": "Avery\u2019s upcoming authored first encounter is shaped by a cautious, resource-conserving mindset, anchored in the persistence of his two signature companions: Caterpie and Metapod. With no new levels, items, or acquisitions available, the strategy must rely entirely on existing tools\u2014String Shot for speed control, Harden for physical bulk, and Effect Nightmare for stall-based damage. The legal preparation envelope permits only minor move adjustments, so any changes should prioritize utility over novelty. Given the reported past battle involving a Bulbasaur, Avery may anticipate grass-type opponents, but without current intelligence, this remains speculative. His moderate adaptability suggests he will favor a defensive opening, using Metapod\u2019s Harden to absorb initial hits while Caterpie applies String Shot to dictate tempo. With zero healing items, attrition is a real risk; thus, prolonging battles through status and durability is likely the intended path. Uncertainty looms over the opponent\u2019s lead and move pool\u2014especially unrevealed parties and future input\u2014so the plan must remain flexible within the constraints of the fixed roster. Avery\u2019s pride in his bug-types implies a refusal to abandon them, even under pressure. The strategy is not about aggression but endurance: outlast, debuff, and wait for opponent mistakes. Predictions may falter if the enemy carries super-effective coverage or priority moves, but within known parameters, the approach is sound. This is not a gamble\u2014it is a calculated stand by a trainer who values consistency over spectacle.",
